#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286123 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4df33ff-e04e-55ec-b273-9eceff7db53b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rotation Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf3c118a-93f1-5a86-bf30-b0f8eaf85b3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/e3fe0bfa8161108c3d5edc48a6df4a52fe2c5b4dbf1c9964cf82e4f257ff357c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286125} {:answer/id #uuid "e20e2989-5197-5f02-89fc-96cda30ba61f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/cf449d44237c85963bf4fbb134da290b39aac4ebd0b128313052cbd1970db67f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286126} {:answer/id #uuid "87f065e9-8ca0-5637-9ddd-76dec9b86fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/979157d993a86617fabf4b2dfacc6d4c1d973885b42be081b4bcffb36058e091.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286127} {:answer/id #uuid "e4827f5b-a4a1-556a-86e7-4a07bd2d6e9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/4bf42e3bdeb61feccd68cf4eeb9e3c4a40e8b903a5739df77c993e9aa4abc993.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286128} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef96b34-9af2-541f-9f26-8660063b1119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/f4d4d52cb24bd1e3dd4bc37736533693ff89e6b08f495f8541f23abde995a5b9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4827f5b-a4a1-556a-86e7-4a07bd2d6e9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/4bf42e3bdeb61feccd68cf4eeb9e3c4a40e8b903a5739df77c993e9aa4abc993.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286128} :answer-field/id #uuid "e433f5d2-bb77-5783-a60a-e5781b101597" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b00d738-ec8e-51fc-8984-e5492d98724b" :question/math-academy-id "q-81829" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/df7a1eb6aaf75cc611826af00ce066ed05440bb048ad79d8c0532007b9a89c3a.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors. Computing the images of ${i,j}$ under $A$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =Ai=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =Aj=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/77936c4115b37d79ae301a93b218ecd23114ae4ad42d8298b8f058c1f50e82a2.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians **clockwise** about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ **clockwise** by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/e941207a92a2b688428c55be3bc17856ea47fa2e11db8e3dc571b88ebbe8e3b1.png)"}]}
